X4 Pro: use the maximum SDMMC data timeout at the current 20 MHz clock.

Targets ESP-IDF 87912cd291d68f4319f13695718af6754879a83f, as shipped by
PioArduino 55.03.37. Related upstream report:
https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf/issues/12968

At the current SDMMC_FREQ_DEFAULT (20 MHz), requesting 839 ms makes the
existing LL setter clamp 16,780,000 cycles to the 24-bit register maximum
of 16,777,215 cycles: 838.86075 ms. Keep the clock unchanged and label the
log as the requested timeout, since the hardware rounds it down slightly.
This does not change the separate command timeout or five-second card-ready
deadline.

diff --git a/esp_driver_sdmmc/src/sdmmc_host.c b/esp_driver_sdmmc/src/sdmmc_host.c
--- a/esp_driver_sdmmc/src/sdmmc_host.c
+++ b/esp_driver_sdmmc/src/sdmmc_host.c
@@ -293,9 +293,11 @@ static int sdmmc_host_calc_freq(soc_periph_sdmmc_clk_src_t src, const int host_div,
 
 static void sdmmc_host_set_data_timeout(uint32_t freq_khz)
 {
-    const uint32_t data_timeout_ms = 100;
+    const uint32_t data_timeout_ms = 839;
     uint32_t data_timeout_cycles = data_timeout_ms * freq_khz;
     sdmmc_ll_set_data_timeout(s_host_ctx.hal.dev, data_timeout_cycles);
+    esp_rom_printf("CrossInk SDMMC: data timeout request=%u ms, requested clock=%u kHz\n",
+                   (unsigned)data_timeout_ms, (unsigned)freq_khz);
 }
 
 esp_err_t sdmmc_host_set_card_clk(int slot, uint32_t freq_khz)
